# UI/UX design (UX spec)

Companion to `frontend-web.mdc` and `architecture-and-diagrams.mdc`. Produced in Design, implemented in Build, audited in Verify.

## UX spec (`docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/ux-spec.md`)

Produced by `ux-designer` (skill `ux-design`) when the change affects a UI surface:

- **User flows** — Mermaid per primary task.
- **Screen inventory + state matrix** — loading, error, empty, success per data surface, each linked to a mockup.
- **HTML mockups** — static files under `docs/agents-v0/design/<feature>/mockups/`. One file per screen state. No API calls. Layout, hierarchy, labels, and visible controls live here.
- **Component defaults** — every interactive component: name, screen, mockup, OpenAPI operation when it calls the API, default behavior, and an override column. Shared components are defined once; screen rows reference that name.
- **Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)** — keyboard, focus, modals, ARIA, contrast, reduced motion, touch targets.
- **Responsive + device matrix** — from Intake.
- **Design-system conformance** — deviations via ADR.
- **UX acceptance criteria** — testable rows mapped to a screen and a mockup (Verify covers each on the built UI).

A screen is not ready when a mockup has no component row, a visible control has no row, a row links to a missing mockup, or the mockup and the row disagree. An override is applied by changing the mockup and the row together. A component that calls the API names an operation in the approved OpenAPI contract. It does not invent an endpoint. The mockup for a result (success, validation error, 401, 5xx) is static. The real client is written in Build.

## Build and Verify

`frontend-engineer` implements the approved spec and component defaults, and matches the linked mockups for layout. API calls live in the app, using the operation named on the component row.

`test-engineer` runs axe-core on changed routes of the built UI and maps each UX acceptance criterion to a test. Results go in `docs/agents-v0/verify/<feature>/ux-report.md`. Mockups are not the test target.
